====Limited editions====
For the [[Italia]]n market, a limited edition Swift Sport BeeRacing was launched in March 2018.<ref>{{cite news |date=15 March 2018 |title=Suzuki Swift Sport, Speciale Bee-Racing |trans-title=Suzuki Swift Sport, Speciale Bee-Racing |url=https://www.patentati.it/blog/articoli-auto/nuova-suzuki-swift-beeracing-edizione-speciale.html |access-date=19 March 2021 |website=patentati.it |language=Italian}}</ref> In June of the same year, 100 units limited edition Swift Sport, called the Red Devil was announced for the [[Australia]]n market.<ref>{{cite press release|url=https://www.suzuki.com.au/suzuki-life/news/swift-sport-limited-edition-red-devil-announced|title=Swift Sport Limited Edition Red Devil Announced|date=13 June 2018|access-date=19 March 2021|work=Suzuki Australia}}</ref>

In May 2019, a limited edition Swift Sport Katana was launched for [[Netherlands|Dutch]] market only. The limited edition [[hot hatch]] pays tribute to the new [[Suzuki Katana#Suzuki Katana 1000|Suzuki Katana 1000]] bike. Built in a limited run of only 30 units, it comes in two colors, 15 units Premium Silver Metallic and 15 units Super Black Pearl paints.<ref>{{cite web |last=Mihalascu |first=Dan |date=2019-05-07 |title=Suzuki Swift Sport Katana Is A Dutch-Only Limited Edition Model |url=https://www.carscoops.com/2019/05/suzuki-swift-sport-katana-is-a-dutch-only-limited-edition-model/ |website=Carscoops}}</ref><ref>{{cite press release |title=NIEUW EXCLUSIEF TOPMODEL SUZUKI SWIFT: DE SWIFT SPORT KATANA |url=https://www.suzuki.nl/auto-versteeg-buurman-ermelo/nieuws/persberichten/swift/30-04-2019-swift-sport-katana/# |language=nl |trans-title=NEW EXCLUSIVE TOP MODEL SUZUKI SWIFT: THE SWIFT SPORT KATANA |work=Suzuki Netherlands}}</ref>

Another limited edition for Italian market was launched in February 2021 to celebrate [[Suzuki MotoGP]]'s 7th world championship title after [[Joan Mir]] won the [[2020 MotoGP season]]. Dubbed as the World Champion Edition and only 7 units were available for sale.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.visordown.com/news/general/suzuki-celebrates-motogp-glory-swift-hybrid-world-champion-edition|title=SUZUKI CELEBRATES MOTOGP GLORY WITH SWIFT HYBRID WORLD CHAMPION EDITION|first=Simon|last=Hancocks|date=15 February 2021|access-date=19 March 2021|work=Visor Down}}</ref>

Malaysian market received a limited edition called Silver Edition in October 2023. Compared to regular Swift Sport, the hatchback received additional styling upgrades such as exclusive metallic silver body color, red accents, carbon fiber finish and bigger {{cvt|10|in|order=flip}} LCD screen.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://paultan.org/2023/10/30/2023-suzuki-swift-sport-silver-edition-launched-in-malaysia/|title=2023 Suzuki Swift Sport Silver Edition launched in Malaysia – sportier styling; 10-inch HU; from RM146k|first=Gerard | last = Lye|date=30 October 2023|publisher=Paul Tan's Automotive News}}</ref>

In 2019, Japanese tuner [[Tommykaira]] launched a tuned car based on the ZC33S Swift Sport called the '''Tommykaira m14''', 12 years after the ZC31S Swift Sport-based S-Ss had been introduced in 2007.<ref name="tommykaira"/> It was available in three packages; Stage I, Stage II and Stage III.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://gtst.jp/tommykaira/m14/|title=Tommykaira m14|language=Japanese|website=gtst.jp}}</ref>

===Special and limited editions===
Similar special or limited editions of Swift with Japanese market honeycomb grille, front and rear spoiler, sidekirts, decals (depending on the markets) and additional accessories were launched in [[India]], [[Philippines]], [[South Africa]], [[Australia]], [[United Kingdom]] and several other markets.<ref>{{cite web |last=Nadkarny |first=Aditya |date=10 October 2020 |title=Maruti Suzuki Swift special edition launched in India |url=https://www.carwale.com/news/maruti-suzuki-swift-special-edition-launched-in-india/ |website=CarWale}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://jamesdeakin.ph/blog/suzuki-ph-takes-all-new-swift-trip-down-memory-lane-las-casas-bataan|title=Suzuki PH takes the all-new Swift on a trip down memory lane at Las Casas in Bataan|date=6 April 2019|website=jamesdeakin.ph}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Lilleike |first=Gero |date=11 November 2019 |title=Suzuki Launches Special Edition Swift, Ignis in SA |url=https://www.cars.co.za/motoring-news/suzuki-launches-special-edition-swift-ignis-in-sa/77792/ |website=Cars.co.za}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Misoyannis |first=Alex |date=1 April 2021 |title=2021 Suzuki Swift 100 Year Anniversary Edition price and specs |url=https://www.caradvice.com.au/939456/2021-suzuki-swift-100-year-anniversary-edition-price-and-specs/ |website=Drive}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Ingram |first=Alex |date=12 July 2019 |title=New Suzuki Swift Attitude 2019 review |url=https://www.autoexpress.co.uk/suzuki/swift/107426/new-suzuki-swift-attitude-2019-review |website=Auto Express}}</ref>

A special edition based on XG trim called XR Limited was launched for Japanese market in October 2018. The car received sporty exterior package from RS trim, additional "Suzuki Safety Support" safety kits and several comfort features from higher trim.<ref>{{cite press release |title=スズキ、小型乗用車「スイフト」に 特別仕様車「XRリミテッド」を設定して発売 |date=11 October 2018 |url=https://www.suzuki.co.jp/release/a/2018/1011/ |language=Japanese |trans-title=Suzuki launches special edition "XR Limited" of compact passenger car "Swift" |work=Suzuki Japan}}</ref> Another limited edition based on the updated XG trim was launched in November 2019, called the Hybrid MG Limited. Basically the car has similar package as the previous limited edition but without sporty RS trim bumpers and additional mild hybrid system as standard.<ref>{{cite press release |title=スズキ、小型乗用車「スイフト」に 特別仕様車「HYBRID MGリミテッド」を設定して発売 |date=14 November 2019 |url=https://www.suzuki.co.jp/release/a/2019/1114/ |language=Japanese |trans-title=Suzuki launches special edition "HYBRID MG Limited" of its compact passenger car "Swift" |work=Suzuki Japan}}</ref>

In Thailand, a special edition called Swift GL Max Edition was launched in November 2020. Equipped with black colored body kit, crossover-like flare fenders, shark fin antenna and decorated quad exhaust pipes.<ref>{{cite web |date=5 November 2020 |title=Suzuki Swift GL Max Edition launched in Thailand |url=https://namastecar.com/suzuki-swift-gl-max-edition-launched-in-thailand/ |website=NamasteCar}}</ref> Another special edition with different body kit called GL Plus was launched in August 2021,<ref>{{cite press release |title="ซซก" ตอกยำภาพลกษณสปอรตอโคคาร แนะนำ 'SUZUKI SWIFT GL PLUS' |date=21 August 2021 |url=https://www.suzuki.co.th/news/articles/news-91 |language=Thai |access-date=25 September 2021 |trans-title="Ssok" reinforces the image of a sports car, introducing 'SUZUKI SWIFT GL PLUS' |work=Suzuki Thailand}}</ref> and limited edition with upgraded body kit called GL Plus Limitless Edition was launched in June 2022.<ref>{{cite press release |title=NEW SUZUKI SWIFT GL PLUS อัพเกรดชุดแต่งรอบคัน เวอร์ชันพิเศษ Limitless Edition ตอกย้ำภาพลักษณ์สปอร์ตแฮทช์แบ็กคาร์ ในราคา 572,000 บาท |date=21 June 2022 |url=https://www.suzuki.co.th/news/articles/news-110 |language=Thai |access-date=9 July 2022 |trans-title=NEW SUZUKI SWIFT GL PLUS upgrades the body kit, special version Limitless Edition, reinforcing the image of a sports hatchback car at a price of 572,000 baht. |work=Suzuki Thailand}}</ref>

In New Zealand, limited editions called SR, SR2 and SR3 with similar concept as the previous generations Swift were available from 2018 to 2021. The most notable changes were the wider 205/45 sport tires and 17-inch black alloy wheels.<ref>{{cite web |date=10 May 2018 |title=New SR Adds Cutting Edge to Popular Suzuki Swift |url=https://www.suzuki.co.nz/cars/suzuki-life/news/article/new-sr-adds-cutting-edge-to-popular-suzuki-swift/556074 |website=Suzuki New Zealand}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=12 July 2019 |title=The limited edition Suzuki Swift SR2, have fun and look sharp |url=https://www.facebook.com/SuzukiNZ/posts/2463729017020938 |url-access=limited |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/iarchive/facebook/206160382777824/2463729017020938 |archive-date=2022-02-26 |website=Facebook}}{{cbignore}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Alvrez |first=Fred |date=10 February 2021 |title=New model Suzuki Swift – the SR3 – available now |url=https://www.drivelife.co.nz/2021/02/new-model-suzuki-swift-the-sr3-available-now/ |website=DriveLife}}</ref>

