=== Markets ===

=== Asia ===

==== India ====
The fourth-generation Swift made its Indian debut on 9 May 2024, with five trim levels: LXi, VXi, VXi (O), ZXi and ZXi+ with either a 5-speed [[manual gearbox]] or a 5-speed [[Automated manual transmission|AMT "AGS"]] , it is powered by the 1.2-liter gasoline engine.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2024-05-09 |title=New Maruti Swift 2024 launched in India: Check price, features, mileage and more |url=https://www.businesstoday.in/auto/story/new-maruti-swift-2024-launched-in-india-check-price-features-mileage-and-more-428890-2024-05-09 |access-date=2024-10-02 |website=Business Today |language=en}}</ref> A CNG option with manual transmission only was launched on 12 September 2024.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2024-10-01 |title=Maruti car sales in September sees slight increase with boost from CNG vehicles |url=https://auto.hindustantimes.com/auto/cars/maruti-car-sales-in-september-sees-slight-increase-with-boost-from-cng-vehicles/-41727786502465.html |access-date=2024-10-02 |website=HT Auto |language=en}}</ref>

Test mules of the performance-oriented Swift Sport based on the fourth-generation Swift have been spotted undergoing road testing in 2025–2026, indicating that a new model could be introduced in the near future.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Next-Gen Suzuki Swift Sport Spotted Testing |url=https://gaadigyaani.com/next-gen-suzuki-swift-sport-launch-2026/ |access-date=13 March 2026}}</ref>

==== Japan ====
The fourth-generation Swift was released in Japan on 13 December 2023, with three variants: XG, Hybrid MX and Hybrid MZ. For engines, the XG is powered by the 1.2-liter gasoline, while the MX and MZ variants powered by the 1.2-liter gasoline mild-hybrid. All three variants have the option between front-wheel drive and all-wheel drive configurations.<ref>{{Cite press release |title=スズキ、小型乗用車 新型「スイフト」を発売 |date=2023-12-06 |publisher=Suzuki Japan |url=https://www.suzuki.co.jp/release/a/2023/1206/ |trans-title=Suzuki launches new compact car "Swift"}}</ref>

==== Taiwan ====
The fourth-generation Swift was launched in Taiwan on 10 July 2024, in the sole variant powered by a 1.2-liter gasoline MHEV engine.<ref>{{Cite web |title=售價73萬元、單一車型設定，Suzuki大改款Swift正式上市 |trans-title=Priced at 730,000 yuan and available as a single model, the redesigned Suzuki Swift has officially launched. |url=https://news.u-car.com.tw/news/article/78782 |access-date=2025-12-26 |website=U-CAR汽車網站 |language=ZH-tw}}</ref>

==== Vietnam ====
The fourth-generation Swift was launched in Vietnam on 26 June 2025, in the sole variant powered by a 1.2-liter gasoline MHEV engine.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Minh |first=Quốc |date=2025-06-26 |title=Suzuki Swift 2025 ra mắt Việt Nam: Giá 569 triệu, máy hybrid, 6 tính năng ADAS, đấu Mazda2 hatchback |trans-title=Suzuki Swift 2025 launched in Vietnam: Price 569 million, hybrid engine, 6 ADAS features, competing with Mazda2 hatchback |url=https://autopro.com.vn/suzuki-swift-2025-ra-mat-viet-nam-gia-569-trieu-may-hybrid-6-tinh-nang-adas-dau-mazda2-hatchback-177250626111528615.chn |access-date=2025-06-27 |website=AutoPro |language=vi}}</ref>

===== Singapore =====

The fourth-generation Swift was launched in Singapore on 8 August 2025, in 2 variants, the DualJet standard variant, and the DualJet Standard (Two-tone) variant. 

Both variants are powered by a 1.2-litre three-cylinder engine putting out 82bhp and 112Nm of torque, paired with a 12-volt mild hybrid system, featuring a combined fuel consumption of 20.4km/L, and equipped with Suzuki Safety Support.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2024-08-08 |title=All-new Suzuki Swift arrives in Singapore|url=https://www.sgcarmart.com/articles/news/all-new-suzuki-swift-arrives-in-singapore-35591 |access-date=2026-03-19 |website=sgcarmart.com |language=en-us}}</ref>

==== Europe ====
The fourth-generation Swift for the European debut in the first quarter of 2024. The Swift for the European market is identical to the Japanese-specification with a few differences such as a simplified front bumper design and the omission of both the front lip and front foglights. For the European market, it is only available with the 1.2-liter gasoline mild-hybrid engine.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-07-12 |title=Fourth-Gen Suzuki Swift MHEV Breaks Cover in Europe |url=https://www.carz.com.my/2023/12/fourth-gen-suzuki-swift-mhev-breaks-cover-in-europe |access-date=2024-09-28 |website=Carz Automedia Malaysia |language=en}}</ref>

==== Mexico ====
The fourth-generation Swift was launched in Mexico on 31 May 2024, in two trim levels: GLS and GLX, it is powered by a 1.2-liter gasoline mild-hybrid engine.<ref>{{Cite web |last=García |first=Gerardo |date=2024-05-31 |title=El Suzuki Swift 2025 ya tiene precio en México: adiós al turbo, hola a una gama 100% mild-hybrid y más seguridad |trans-title=The 2025 Suzuki Swift is now priced in Mexico: goodbye to the turbo, hello to a 100% mild-hybrid range and more safety. |url=https://www.motorpasion.com.mx/industria/suzuki-swift-2025-precio-mexico |access-date=2024-09-28 |website=Motorpasión México |language=es}}</ref>

==== Middle East ====
The fourth-generation Swift was launched in the [[Gulf Cooperation Council|GCC]] countries on 25 November 2024, in three trim levels; GL, GL Plus and GLX, it is powered by the 1.2-liter gasoline mild-hybrid engine.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Chowdhury |first=Marouf Hussain |date=2024-11-27 |title=2025 Suzuki Swift Launches in the UAE |url=https://www.drivearabia.com/news/2024/11/27/2025-suzuki-swift-launches-in-the-uae/ |access-date=2024-12-14 |website=Drive Arabia |language=en-US}}</ref>

==== Oceania ====

===== Australia =====
The fourth-generation Swift was launched in Australia on 14 June 2024, with four variants: Hybrid (M/T), Hybrid (CVT), Hybrid Plus and Hybrid GLX, it is powered by the 1.2-liter gasoline mild-hybrid engine.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wong |first=James |date=2024-06-14 |title=2024 Suzuki Swift Hybrid price and specs |url=https://www.carexpert.com.au/car-news/2024-suzuki-swift-hybrid-price-and-specs |access-date=2024-09-27 |website=CarExpert |language=en}}</ref>

===== New Zealand =====
The fourth-generation Swift was launched in New Zealand on 7 June 2024, in two trim levels: GLS and RSC, it is powered by a 1.2-liter gasoline engine.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Alvárez |first=Fred |date=2024-06-06 |title=2024 Suzuki Swift launch |url=https://www.drivelife.co.nz/2024/06/2024-suzuki-swift-launch/ |access-date=2024-09-27 |website=DriveLife |language=en-GB}}</ref>

==== South Africa ====
The fourth-generation Swift was launched in South Africa on 27 September 2024, in three trim levels: GL, GL+ and GLX, it is powered by the 1.2-liter gasoline engine.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Du Toit |first=Albert |date=2024-09-27 |title=New Suzuki Swift – South African pricing and specifications announced |url=https://topauto.co.za/news/116298/new-suzuki-swift-south-african-pricing-and-specifications-announced/ |work=TopAuto}}</ref>

=== Powertrain ===
A brand new 1.2-liter three-cylinder engine called ''[[List of Suzuki engines#Z engine|Z12E]]'' was also introduced, replacing the older ''[[Suzuki K engine|K12D/N Dualjet]]'' four-cylinder engines and available in conventional or mild hybrid versions. It is mated to a 5-speed manual transmission or a newly developed lightweight CVT, available for both front or all-wheel drive configurations. A 5-speed automated manual transmission ''Auto Gear Shift (AGS)'' is also available mainly for Indian market.
A CNG variant of the ''Z12E'' engine was introduced in India in September 2024.<ref>{{cite press release|url=https://www.marutisuzuki.com/corporate/media/press-releases/2024/september/epic-new-swift-s-cng|title=Maruti Suzuki launches the Epic New Swift S-CNG; most fuel-efficient hatchback in its segment|date=12 September 2024|publisher=Maruti Suzuki}}</ref>

